  "result": "The gate returned **OK** on the first run (1 of 6 used): all 3 witnesses passed, and the body reads the 2 atoms the record claims.\n\n**Concept body** (`library/TrafficSpec/Concepts/motion/backing.lean`): it checks that the vehicle's velocity along its heading is below minus the motion tolerance:\n\n`(vx·hx + vy·hy) < −motion_tolerance`\n\n- vx, vy come from `kin_velocity` and hx, hy from `kin_heading`; Core reads the heading as a unit vector.\n- The gear is not read, as the record says.\n- The comparison is strict because the contract says \"lying below\". That follows directly from the words, so I declared no narrowing.\n\n**Witnesses** (`library/TrafficSpecWitness/Concepts/motion/backing.lean`): the tolerance is set to 10 cm/s. The vehicle points east and is in reverse gear in every scenario.\n- **holds:** it rolls west at 2 m/s, so its velocity along the heading is −2 m/s.\n- **fails:** it stands still, so that value is 0.\n- **blind:** the holds scene, with `kin.velocity` declared absent.\n\nThe gate runs and the reasoning behind each choice are in `task_result.md` in the working directory.",
